        <body>
            <div xml:id="d234">

                <pb facs="0304" n="1038" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1038"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gibbs to Mr. Evarts.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-07-24"><hi rendition="#italic">July 24, 1878</hi></date>.
                        (Received Aug. 19.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 268.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to refer to my dispatch No. 245, in
                    relation to claims of Mr. Thomas W. Sparrow and others for salaries due by the
                    Peruvian Government for services rendered in the Hydrographic Commission on the
                    Amazon River.</p>
                <p>On the 6th instant I passed a note to the minister of foreign affairs, as per
                    copy, and sent with it various documents in relation to these claims.</p>
                <p>Yesterday I received an answer (copy inclosed), with translation, but I perceive
                    that the honorable minister has included the name of J. R. Tucker. This is an
                    error, as I did not mention that name in any of the notes passed. I now expect
                    that the amounts will be paid, but I will still keep the claims in mind, and
                    will learn if the promise has been carried out.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Gibbs.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d234-a1.xml" xpointer="d234-a1"/>
